1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:02,419
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:47,965
THE PERFECT LIE

3
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,638
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

4
00:00:54,721 --> 00:00:57,975
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS
AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

5
00:00:58,642 --> 00:01:00,644
[♪ ominous music playing]

6
00:01:30,173 --> 00:01:31,592
[softly] No, that can't be…

7
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:42,519
[clicks tongue] What I do know is,

8
00:01:42,603 --> 00:01:45,480
just because we kissed doesn't mean
I wanted to have sex with him.

9
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:51,403
Right at that moment,
my phone alarm went off.

10
00:01:53,238 --> 00:01:58,660
With daylight saving time in effect,
the US stock market opens at 10:30 p.m.

11
00:02:02,372 --> 00:02:03,457
[Junho taps on phone]

12
00:02:06,376 --> 00:02:07,377
Here, you can check.

13
00:02:17,512 --> 00:02:18,555
[phone alarm sounds]

14
00:02:24,019 --> 00:02:25,020
[alarm intensifies]

15
00:02:27,022 --> 00:02:28,023
[sinister sting]

16
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:34,655
EPISODE 2
THAT NIGHT

17
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:36,198
[detective] What happened after the kiss?

18
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:38,659
[Junho exhales sharply]

19
00:02:38,742 --> 00:02:40,994
This is ridiculous.
How am I supposed to tell you?

20
00:02:41,078 --> 00:02:42,788
[team leader]
She said it was sexual assault.

21
00:02:43,497 --> 00:02:44,498
No.

22
00:02:56,093 --> 00:02:57,636
We sat on the couch,

23
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:01,473
had some wine, and talked some more.

24
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:02,641
[typing]

25
00:03:03,558 --> 00:03:05,936
Then Ms. Kang took me to the bedroom.

26
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:13,235
Do I really have to go
into every single detail?

27
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:14,945
[detective]
<i>And after you went into the bedroom?</i>

28
00:03:17,781 --> 00:03:18,782
[Junho sighs]

29
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:24,287
We lay down on the bed together.

30
00:03:24,788 --> 00:03:26,706
[♪ tense music plays]

31
00:03:33,922 --> 00:03:35,674
[detective]
Were you on top of her, Mr. Min?

32
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:39,469
Yes.

33
00:03:40,679 --> 00:03:42,097
Did you push her down?

34
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,434
No, I did not.

35
00:03:45,517 --> 00:03:46,601
I told him to stop.

36
00:03:46,685 --> 00:03:49,479
I really… I really didn't want it!

37
00:03:49,563 --> 00:03:50,814
[sobbing]

38
00:03:50,897 --> 00:03:52,816
I really didn't want to do it.

39
00:03:52,899 --> 00:03:55,193
[crying, breathing shakily]

40
00:03:59,406 --> 00:04:00,574
We kissed and…

41
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:03,368
just naturally…

42
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,789
I swear, it wasn't a situation
where she'd feel uncomfortable.

43
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:10,250
<i>If anything, it was the opposite.</i>

44
00:04:11,251 --> 00:04:14,963
<i>Ms. Kang never pushed me away or resisted.</i>

45
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:19,342
Not once did she tell me to stop.

46
00:04:20,927 --> 00:04:23,013
[crying] I don't remember.

47
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:26,433
I don't know when it started.

48
00:04:35,233 --> 00:04:36,693
[♪ somber music plays]

49
00:04:36,777 --> 00:04:38,195
If I'd known Ms. Kang…

50
00:04:40,447 --> 00:04:41,865
didn't want it…

51
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,952
I never would've crossed that line.

52
00:04:49,164 --> 00:04:51,166
<i>I don't know why</i>
<i>she's suddenly doing this.</i>

53
00:04:58,298 --> 00:05:00,884
My feelings were genuine.
[inhales sharply]

54
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:02,677
[sighs]

55
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:05,722
I wanted to keep seeing her…

56
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:11,186
Maybe even build a future…

57
00:05:12,646 --> 00:05:13,647
[sighs]

58
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:19,736
I texted her in the morning

59
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:22,113
and even had
some porridge delivered to her.

60
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:25,116
- We confirmed that.
- [typing]

61
00:05:26,243 --> 00:05:29,621
I mean, if we really didn't have
a good time last night,

62
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,748
I wouldn't have sent her
a text like that, would I?

63
00:05:33,875 --> 00:05:35,877
If something like that
had actually happened…

64
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:38,922
it makes no sense.

65
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,676
[Soyeon] <i>Why Ms. Kang of all people?</i>

66
00:05:44,386 --> 00:05:45,554
Because we're close.

67
00:05:45,637 --> 00:05:47,514
Did you really not tell her the truth?

68
00:05:48,974 --> 00:05:50,141
About what?

69
00:05:50,225 --> 00:05:53,645
That I'm the one who sold the sneakers,
and that you just let me use your account.

70
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,820
You like me, don't you?

71
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:03,780
No, I don't.

72
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:06,199
Then why did you give me this?

73
00:06:06,283 --> 00:06:07,367
Is it a knockoff?

74
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:09,119
It's real, okay?

75
00:06:09,202 --> 00:06:10,620
Then why did you give it to me?

76
00:06:12,664 --> 00:06:14,833
Your shoes and your bag are all knockoffs.

77
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:19,004
I thought you should have
at least one real thing…

78
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:20,171
[chuckles]

79
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:23,717
[Soyeon] See? You do like me.

80
00:06:25,135 --> 00:06:26,386
I told you, I don't.

81
00:06:26,887 --> 00:06:27,888
[Soyeon laughs softly]

82
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:31,474
Sex crime cases--

83
00:06:31,558 --> 00:06:32,851
It wasn't a crime.

84
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:39,357
You're sure it wasn't?

85
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:42,986
Yeah, I'm sure.

86
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:47,699
Being too perfect is a crime too.

87
00:06:50,452 --> 00:06:52,495
I know you're someone
who wouldn't do that,

88
00:06:53,413 --> 00:06:55,540
but I'm asking as your attorney.

89
00:07:00,879 --> 00:07:01,880
You…

90
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:03,506
don't believe me?

91
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,135
Okay, fine.

92
00:07:07,886 --> 00:07:09,095
Then I'll represent you.

93
00:07:10,138 --> 00:07:11,181
No need.

94
00:07:11,264 --> 00:07:14,309
Hey, you don't hire an attorney
to cover up lies.

95
00:07:14,392 --> 00:07:16,353
You hire one to protect the truth.

96
00:07:19,522 --> 00:07:20,523
- [sighs]
- First,

97
00:07:20,607 --> 00:07:22,567
I'll find out why
that woman is doing this.

98
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:25,445
- [door closes]
- [kids] Mom!

99
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:26,529
[Jieun] Hey.

100
00:07:26,613 --> 00:07:28,448
- [Ugeun] Yay, Auntie's here!
- [Uyeong] Yay, Auntie!

101
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,866
[Jieun] You didn't put them to bed?

102
00:07:29,949 --> 00:07:31,493
- [kids chattering]
- They wanted to see you first.

103
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:35,288
Wow, you did such a good job.
But it's way past your bedtime.

104
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:37,540
- Auntie's here to sleep too.
- [parent] All right, bedtime.

105
00:07:37,624 --> 00:07:39,501
- Play with Auntie tomorrow, okay?
- [parent] Let's go.

106
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,586
But how come you came together?

107
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:44,589
[Jieun] Uh, Jisun wasn't feeling too well.

108
00:07:45,423 --> 00:07:47,050
What's wrong? Are you sick?

109
00:07:48,093 --> 00:07:49,678
Oh, it's nothing. I just…

110
00:07:50,387 --> 00:07:51,554
[Jieun] Go on up.

111
00:07:57,769 --> 00:07:59,688
I told her to come and stay with us.

112
00:07:59,771 --> 00:08:01,481
I didn't feel right leaving her alone.

113
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:02,857
- Oh…
- [Jieun] Yeah.

114
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:06,986
[♪ tense music plays]

115
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:08,071
[sighs]

116
00:08:27,507 --> 00:08:28,508
[gasps softly]

117
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:31,010
Sorry.

118
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:33,680
- No, it's okay.
- [Jieun] Hmm.

119
00:08:34,597 --> 00:08:36,891
I put some blankets
and a pillow over there.

120
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:40,437
Thanks.

121
00:08:41,855 --> 00:08:43,440
I'm so glad I have you.

122
00:08:45,567 --> 00:08:46,568
[Jieun sighs]

123
00:08:47,444 --> 00:08:48,903
Give me your door code.

124
00:08:48,987 --> 00:08:51,239
I'll go get some things you might need.

125
00:08:52,866 --> 00:08:54,868
[♪ tense music plays]

126
00:08:58,079 --> 00:08:59,372
[phone buzzing]

127
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:04,294
[sighs]

128
00:09:07,255 --> 00:09:09,257
- [taps phone]
- [phone buzzing stops]

129
00:09:34,616 --> 00:09:35,617
[sighs]

130
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:01,976
[door closes]

131
00:10:03,561 --> 00:10:04,562
[footsteps approaching]

132
00:10:06,189 --> 00:10:09,192
[detective] You know what DFSA is, right?

133
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,653
You're a doctor, so I'm sure you do.

134
00:10:12,654 --> 00:10:14,072
What does that mean?

135
00:10:14,155 --> 00:10:16,241
Drug-facilitated sexual assault.

136
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:19,077
- The so-called "date-rape drugs."
- [scoffs]

137
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,040
Why are you telling me this?

138
00:10:28,002 --> 00:10:32,507
Ms. Kang Jisun's
toxicology screening results are in.

139
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:40,431
[sighs]

140
00:10:41,558 --> 00:10:42,559
[gasps]

141
00:10:44,435 --> 00:10:45,436
[breathing heavily]

142
00:11:03,705 --> 00:11:05,707
[breathing shakily]

143
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:42,118
You're eating breakfast pretty late.

144
00:11:45,705 --> 00:11:47,081
[Hyunsoo] You're just getting home now?

145
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:50,210
Yeah, I had a lot of surgeries yesterday.

146
00:11:51,502 --> 00:11:53,463
- [liquid pouring]
- I figured.

147
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:57,091
Sorry I couldn't call.

148
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:07,644
Dad, are you okay?

149
00:12:07,727 --> 00:12:08,728
[Junho] What?

150
00:12:09,354 --> 00:12:11,773
[chuckles] I'm just a little tired.

151
00:12:20,657 --> 00:12:23,117
Hyunsoo, the truth is…

152
00:12:27,622 --> 00:12:30,458
Hey, why haven't you changed yet?

153
00:12:31,459 --> 00:12:32,752
It's Saturday.

154
00:12:37,382 --> 00:12:38,383
Oh.

155
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:40,593
Right.

156
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:56,651
[whispers] Jisun.

157
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:01,531
Jisun.

158
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:03,866
Hmm.

159
00:13:05,785 --> 00:13:07,203
What time is it?

160
00:13:08,413 --> 00:13:10,873
[Jieun] A little after 3:00 p.m.

161
00:13:12,583 --> 00:13:15,837
How can you keep sleeping
like this without eating?

162
00:13:18,214 --> 00:13:20,258
I brought some food,

163
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:22,593
so eat something
then go back to sleep, okay?

164
00:13:22,677 --> 00:13:23,678
[Jisun] Okay.

165
00:13:29,809 --> 00:13:31,602
[♪ melancholic music plays]

166
00:13:36,691 --> 00:13:38,693
[soft ticking]

167
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:53,166
[sighs]

168
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:01,549
[soft ticking continues]

169
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,401
[parent] Aren't you going to tell me
what's going on with Jisun?

170
00:14:21,903 --> 00:14:23,071
I told you already.

171
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,532
- [Uyeong] Dad, I need a straw!
- Oh, boy.

172
00:14:27,325 --> 00:14:29,786
Goodness, where are the wet wipes?

173
00:14:32,789 --> 00:14:36,334
Gosh, you little mess. [chuckles]

174
00:14:36,417 --> 00:14:38,461
- Here.
- [Jieun] Gosh, you.

175
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:41,589
[parent] Now, don't spill and enjoy.

176
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:43,508
Go on and watch TV.

177
00:14:49,972 --> 00:14:52,683
Come on. I know she's not just sick.

178
00:14:54,143 --> 00:14:56,145
Is it something you need to hide from me?

179
00:14:59,524 --> 00:15:00,817
Don't let anyone know, okay?

180
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,361
[parent] Okay.

181
00:15:03,444 --> 00:15:05,113
[♪ unsettling music plays]

182
00:15:05,196 --> 00:15:08,741
She went on a date
with Dr. Min Junho from our hospital,

183
00:15:08,825 --> 00:15:10,535
the one she told us about before.

184
00:15:10,618 --> 00:15:11,702
Oh, really?

185
00:15:12,495 --> 00:15:13,496
And?

186
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:16,499
[no audible dialogue]

187
00:15:20,336 --> 00:15:22,547
[♪ unsettling music continues]

188
00:15:32,265 --> 00:15:33,891
I seriously can't believe it.

189
00:15:35,101 --> 00:15:37,103
Do the police know
about what happened before?

190
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:39,397
Why would they need to know?

191
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:41,607
- [parent] Well…
- [footsteps approaching]

192
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,945
[Jieun] Hey, did you get some sleep?

193
00:15:46,028 --> 00:15:47,029
I'm going to work.

194
00:15:47,113 --> 00:15:50,074
Have some breakfast before you go.

195
00:15:50,158 --> 00:15:51,325
No, I'm good.

196
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:53,578
[Jieun] Hey, Jisun.

197
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:57,290
I think you should take
a few more days off.

198
00:16:01,419 --> 00:16:02,420
I'm okay.

199
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:04,338
I need to get on with my life.

200
00:16:11,679 --> 00:16:12,972
[teacher] Your sister called.

201
00:16:14,557 --> 00:16:16,517
Were you so sick you couldn't even call?

202
00:16:17,351 --> 00:16:18,519
I'm sorry.

203
00:16:19,562 --> 00:16:20,730
[teacher] What was wrong?

204
00:16:21,439 --> 00:16:22,857
How sick were you?

205
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:26,861
Well…

206
00:16:29,197 --> 00:16:30,615
I'm sorry.

207
00:16:32,909 --> 00:16:35,411
[sighs]
Next time, no matter how sick you are,

208
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:36,495
call me yourself.

209
00:16:38,164 --> 00:16:40,374
You're a teacher.
You can't just miss work.

210
00:16:41,334 --> 00:16:42,460
Understood?

211
00:16:43,294 --> 00:16:44,295
Yes.

212
00:16:46,380 --> 00:16:50,009
[teacher] I'll put it down as sick leave
and talk to the vice principal.

213
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:53,054
Oh, right.
You <i>are</i> teaching during class, right?

214
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:56,641
Yes.

215
00:16:56,724 --> 00:17:00,770
These days, parents send their kids
with recording devices.

216
00:17:00,853 --> 00:17:04,941
Treat every class like the parents
are sitting in and observing.

217
00:17:07,151 --> 00:17:08,903
You understand what I'm saying, right?

218
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,614
Yes, I understand.

219
00:17:20,122 --> 00:17:23,334
Soyeon, you must've been busy.
But you still managed to finish the book.

220
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:25,711
I read it in the car, while on the move.

221
00:17:27,505 --> 00:17:28,589
That's dedication.

222
00:17:53,489 --> 00:17:54,699
Here.

223
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:55,950
[Hyunsoo] Ms. Kang.

224
00:17:56,576 --> 00:17:58,077
Mine doesn't have a comment.

225
00:18:03,708 --> 00:18:05,585
There's a reason there isn't one.

226
00:18:06,961 --> 00:18:08,629
- Here you go, Byeongjun.
- [Byeongjun] Thank you.

227
00:18:17,138 --> 00:18:18,139
[sighs]

228
00:18:21,642 --> 00:18:23,311
[♪ unsettling music plays]

229
00:18:27,023 --> 00:18:29,650
- [thud]
- [students clamoring]

230
00:18:32,612 --> 00:18:34,071
[student] Hey! What are you doing?

231
00:18:34,155 --> 00:18:36,157
[clamoring continues]

232
00:18:38,909 --> 00:18:40,411
What are you guys doing? Stop it!

233
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:43,331
Min Hyunsoo, Yeon Sanghyeon, I said stop!

234
00:18:43,414 --> 00:18:44,457
[student 1] Ms. Kang!

235
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:46,083
[Sanghyeon] Let go of me!

236
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:48,169
- [student 2] Let it go!
- [Sanghyeon] Let go!

237
00:18:48,252 --> 00:18:49,629
- Let go of me!
- [student 3] Let it go.

238
00:18:49,712 --> 00:18:51,464
What's going on? Why are you fighting?

239
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:52,548
[student 4] Ms. Kang's here.

240
00:18:56,302 --> 00:18:58,095
I'm asking you what's going on!

241
00:18:58,179 --> 00:18:59,180
[panting]

242
00:19:00,014 --> 00:19:02,016
That bastard hit me first.

243
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:04,935
[Jisun] Is that true? Why did you do that?

244
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:09,940
Do you both want demerits?

245
00:19:10,024 --> 00:19:11,776
I didn't do anything wrong.

246
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:14,945
- I was just stating facts.
- [Hyunsoo] Shut up or I'll kill you!

247
00:19:15,613 --> 00:19:16,614
What did you say?

248
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:18,908
- This bastard's dad is a sex offender.
- What?

249
00:19:18,991 --> 00:19:20,868
My mom saw him getting arrested.

250
00:19:20,951 --> 00:19:22,453
[Hyunsoo] You bastard!

251
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:24,872
- No!
- [student 5] Guys, stop it!

252
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:27,583
[clamoring resumes, fades]

253
00:19:27,667 --> 00:19:29,669
[high-pitched ringing]

254
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:35,549
I've never seen anyone
get taken away in handcuffs before.

255
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:36,967
I know.

256
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:40,179
[sighs] What on earth is going on?

257
00:19:42,223 --> 00:19:44,558
[Junghyeon]
You know, about Dr. Min Junho's wife…

258
00:19:44,642 --> 00:19:46,435
How did she die so young?

259
00:19:46,519 --> 00:19:47,520
Was it an accident?

260
00:19:49,730 --> 00:19:51,857
- [whispering] She took her own life.
- Took her own life?

261
00:19:51,941 --> 00:19:53,192
[♪ somber music plays]

262
00:19:53,275 --> 00:19:54,819
An overdose.

263
00:19:57,321 --> 00:19:58,906
[Junghyeon] An overdose…

264
00:20:08,457 --> 00:20:09,625
[♪ rousing music plays]

265
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:40,322
[rain pattering]

266
00:20:47,955 --> 00:20:48,956
[door lock chimes]

267
00:20:55,004 --> 00:20:56,005
[both chuckle]

268
00:21:04,013 --> 00:21:05,014
[door lock chimes]

269
00:21:21,322 --> 00:21:23,324
[♪ stirring music plays]

270
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:45,471
[shudders]

271
00:21:58,859 --> 00:22:01,904
- [doorbell rings]
- [gasps]

272
00:22:08,994 --> 00:22:10,037
Have a seat.

273
00:22:12,122 --> 00:22:14,500
[detective] You have a nice place.
You even have a yard.

274
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:16,043
[chuckles] Thank you.

275
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:18,045
I saw that you own the place.

276
00:22:19,547 --> 00:22:20,881
It's mostly mortgaged.

277
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:27,638
[team leader] Still, the payments must be
pretty steep to handle on your own.

278
00:22:31,308 --> 00:22:32,309
Well…

279
00:22:32,393 --> 00:22:33,769
It's the same for everyone.

280
00:22:34,562 --> 00:22:36,480
But are you here to check out the house?

281
00:22:37,314 --> 00:22:40,067
Oh, no. Of course not. [inhales sharply]

282
00:22:40,693 --> 00:22:44,488
Uh, Mr. Min has been released for now,
and the investigation is ongoing.

283
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:50,578
[detective] Our job is to uncover
the truth through our investigation.

284
00:22:51,745 --> 00:22:54,748
First of all, neither you nor Mr. Min
had any physical injuries.

285
00:22:54,832 --> 00:22:57,668
How badly do I have to be hurt
for it to count as sexual assault?

286
00:23:03,424 --> 00:23:07,678
The blood test also showed
nothing unusual other than alcohol.

287
00:23:07,761 --> 00:23:11,849
And witnesses at the restaurant said
you seemed to be getting along well.

288
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:15,102
There's also security footage of you
laughing together on your way home.

289
00:23:15,185 --> 00:23:16,812
Because that was before it happened!

290
00:23:17,354 --> 00:23:19,607
Right, but… [inhales sharply]

291
00:23:19,690 --> 00:23:21,400
…aside from your conflicting statements,

292
00:23:21,483 --> 00:23:24,778
we don't have much evidence to go on,
and that's making things difficult for us.

293
00:23:24,862 --> 00:23:27,948
I should take note of that.
Next time, I'll have evidence ready.

294
00:23:33,871 --> 00:23:37,166
Have you had men
come over for drinks before too?

295
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:38,667
No. Never.

296
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:41,503
So having Mr. Min come into your home

297
00:23:41,587 --> 00:23:43,631
- was unusual for you.
- Yes.

298
00:23:43,714 --> 00:23:46,175
If it weren't for the rain,
I never would've let him in!

299
00:23:46,258 --> 00:23:50,179
Mr. Min says you were the one who led him
from the living room into the bedroom.

300
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:51,764
That's a lie!

301
00:23:52,598 --> 00:23:54,600
So it was in bed that you--

302
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:55,684
Yes.

303
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:59,897
You stated that you clearly told him
you didn't want to.

304
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:02,191
- Was that at that point as well?
- Yes! That's why… [sighs]

305
00:24:03,901 --> 00:24:06,111
[♪ tense music plays]

306
00:24:07,529 --> 00:24:08,530
[Jisun sighs]

307
00:24:10,741 --> 00:24:11,784
I couldn't move.

308
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:13,285
I'm not lying!

309
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:16,997
We have to ask as part of the procedure.

310
00:24:19,667 --> 00:24:21,502
I tried to push him away, but I was…

311
00:24:25,881 --> 00:24:28,258
I was so shocked that I couldn't move…

312
00:24:30,844 --> 00:24:33,097
and I don't remember anything
from a certain point.

313
00:24:35,265 --> 00:24:38,936
You were the one
who asked him out to dinner, correct?

314
00:24:39,019 --> 00:24:40,938
I didn't ask him out.
I accepted his invitation!

315
00:24:41,021 --> 00:24:44,149
You were the one who invited him in

316
00:24:44,984 --> 00:24:47,319
and also offered him wine.

317
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:49,863
[scoffs] So?

318
00:24:51,323 --> 00:24:53,033
Does that make it okay?

319
00:25:01,709 --> 00:25:02,710
[car door closes]

320
00:25:11,260 --> 00:25:12,428
[liquid pouring]

321
00:25:12,511 --> 00:25:14,513
[♪ unsettling music plays]

322
00:25:20,853 --> 00:25:21,854
[sighs]

323
00:26:10,277 --> 00:26:11,278
[phone ringing]

324
00:26:14,281 --> 00:26:15,824
- Hey, Jisun.
- Did you clear away

325
00:26:15,908 --> 00:26:17,659
the wine glasses
that were on the coffee table?

326
00:26:18,869 --> 00:26:21,914
[stammers] No, there was nothing there.

327
00:26:22,498 --> 00:26:23,499
[exhales shakily]

328
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:29,713
- [sniffles]
<i>- Why?</i>

329
00:26:30,506 --> 00:26:32,341
<i>- What is it, Jisun?</i>
- [sobbing]

330
00:26:33,050 --> 00:26:34,468
It was the wine.

331
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:37,513
- The wine?
- [breathing shakily]

332
00:26:38,764 --> 00:26:40,599
Did he force you to drink?

333
00:26:40,682 --> 00:26:43,811
Min Junho must've spiked my wine!

334
00:26:43,894 --> 00:26:44,895
[breathing heavily]

335
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:50,567
SEEKING REPORTS FROM VICTIMS

336
00:26:50,651 --> 00:26:53,403
OF DRUG-FACILITATED
SEXUAL ASSAULT SYMPTOMS

337
00:26:53,487 --> 00:26:56,782
AFTER TAKING GHB,
ALSO KNOWN AS A "DATE-RAPE DRUG"

338
00:26:56,865 --> 00:26:58,742
CAN TAKE AWAY EVERYTHING
FROM YOUR MEMORIES

339
00:26:58,826 --> 00:27:01,203
COMMON SYMPTOMS INCLUDE
DIZZINESS, NAUSEA, OR VOMITING

340
00:27:01,286 --> 00:27:03,705
DESPITE NOT HAVING CONSUMED
EXCESSIVE AMOUNTS OF ALCOHOL…

341
00:27:03,789 --> 00:27:05,124
[phone clatters]

342
00:27:08,168 --> 00:27:10,295
[Jisun] I know I left the wine glasses
on the coffee table.

343
00:27:10,379 --> 00:27:12,339
But he washed them
and put them on the rack!

344
00:27:13,799 --> 00:27:16,718
[exhales heavily] No way.
You think he drugged you?

345
00:27:17,344 --> 00:27:19,054
Why else would he wash the glasses?

346
00:27:22,474 --> 00:27:24,017
That's why I couldn't fight back.

347
00:27:24,601 --> 00:27:25,978
That's why I couldn't get away.

348
00:27:26,061 --> 00:27:28,397
And that's why I can't remember anything!

349
00:27:28,480 --> 00:27:30,023
But the test results didn't show--

350
00:27:30,107 --> 00:27:31,608
- I looked it up, and GHB--
- I know.

351
00:27:32,401 --> 00:27:33,986
It leaves your system within a few hours,

352
00:27:34,069 --> 00:27:36,154
and after 12 hours,
there's no trace of it.

353
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:39,116
He planned the whole thing from the start.

354
00:27:40,117 --> 00:27:43,287
A woman who lives alone brought him home
and even gave him wine,

355
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:46,540
so now he can say I'm falsely accusing
an innocent man, a successful doctor!

356
00:27:46,623 --> 00:27:48,458
Jisun, Jisun.

357
00:27:48,542 --> 00:27:50,419
Let's not jump to conclusions.

358
00:27:50,919 --> 00:27:52,421
Like you said,

359
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:55,299
he didn't even know he'd end up
at your place drinking with you.

360
00:27:55,382 --> 00:27:57,426
So the idea that
Dr. Min came prepared with drugs…

361
00:27:58,635 --> 00:28:00,178
Something doesn't add up.

362
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:10,355
[Junho]
You must be really close with your sister.

363
00:28:11,231 --> 00:28:13,525
She mentioned you from time to time.

364
00:28:13,609 --> 00:28:14,610
[♪ slow music plays]

365
00:28:14,693 --> 00:28:16,612
So I knew her sister was a teacher.

366
00:28:18,572 --> 00:28:19,698
That's not fair.

367
00:28:21,074 --> 00:28:22,701
I hardly know anything about you.

368
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:27,205
Other than what everyone else knows,
that you're a respected,

369
00:28:27,289 --> 00:28:29,249
well-known doctor, and a great father.

370
00:28:29,333 --> 00:28:30,334
[chuckles]

371
00:28:33,795 --> 00:28:34,796
[Jisun laughs]

372
00:28:41,303 --> 00:28:43,221
- [crickets chirping]
- [waves crashing]

373
00:29:08,914 --> 00:29:10,457
Can we talk for a minute?

374
00:29:10,540 --> 00:29:12,292
Stay away from me. I'll call the police.

375
00:29:17,839 --> 00:29:20,592
- [Junho] Just let me ask you one thing.
- Stay away! I said stay away!

376
00:29:24,262 --> 00:29:25,389
Why did you do it?

377
00:29:34,106 --> 00:29:35,565
I could ask you the same thing.

378
00:29:39,569 --> 00:29:40,612
Are you really saying…

379
00:29:41,571 --> 00:29:42,572
I forced you?

380
00:29:43,532 --> 00:29:44,658
You're saying you didn't?

381
00:29:44,741 --> 00:29:47,035
I really didn't force you.

382
00:29:47,119 --> 00:29:49,079
You think I wouldn't know?
It happened to me.

383
00:29:49,162 --> 00:29:50,414
It happened to me too.

384
00:29:53,542 --> 00:29:54,626
Jisun…

385
00:29:58,088 --> 00:30:01,842
If I moved too fast, I'm really sorry.

386
00:30:01,925 --> 00:30:03,010
But…

387
00:30:03,969 --> 00:30:06,638
- If you'd told me to stop--
- I did tell you to stop!

388
00:30:11,101 --> 00:30:12,477
No, you didn't.

389
00:30:14,354 --> 00:30:17,816
Maybe you thought it,
but you never said it.

390
00:30:17,899 --> 00:30:19,651
- I did!
- I'm telling you, you didn't!

391
00:30:19,735 --> 00:30:22,446
I'm telling you, I did!
[breathing shakily]

392
00:30:27,325 --> 00:30:28,493
- [Junho sighs]
- [sobs]

393
00:30:29,786 --> 00:30:30,787
[whimpers]

394
00:30:33,582 --> 00:30:35,083
I guess we see things…

395
00:30:37,044 --> 00:30:38,253
very differently.

396
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:39,421
You need to leave.

397
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:41,715
- That day…
- [Jisun gasps]

398
00:30:49,681 --> 00:30:50,932
Why did you meet with me?

399
00:30:52,476 --> 00:30:54,478
[♪ unsettling music plays]

400
00:31:07,824 --> 00:31:10,827
[Junho] <i>I liked you from the start.</i>

401
00:31:11,703 --> 00:31:13,538
<i>From the day we met for the consultation…</i>

402
00:31:13,622 --> 00:31:14,998
<i>No, honestly…</i>

403
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:20,170
from the very first day we met by chance…

404
00:31:22,839 --> 00:31:25,842
I wanted to see you again
for something more serious.

405
00:31:31,306 --> 00:31:34,518
I thought we really clicked.

406
00:31:36,978 --> 00:31:38,814
Didn't you feel the same way?

407
00:31:40,440 --> 00:31:41,441
[chuckles]

408
00:31:44,069 --> 00:31:46,154
I don't know if you remember, but…

409
00:31:48,115 --> 00:31:49,282
that night…

410
00:31:52,494 --> 00:31:54,663
felt so natural.

411
00:31:58,542 --> 00:32:03,672
<i>Honestly,</i>
<i>it was the best night I'd had in years.</i>

412
00:32:08,343 --> 00:32:10,554
- I thought you felt the same way--
- I trusted you.

413
00:32:12,055 --> 00:32:15,308
[crying] I trusted you!

414
00:32:17,394 --> 00:32:19,563
I wanted to be in love!

415
00:32:19,646 --> 00:32:21,648
Not be a victim of a crime!

416
00:32:29,239 --> 00:32:30,448
You're misunderstanding me.

417
00:32:32,409 --> 00:32:34,077
- I really…
- Don't come any closer.

418
00:32:34,161 --> 00:32:35,579
Don't come any closer!

419
00:32:40,917 --> 00:32:42,210
Jisun…

420
00:32:48,091 --> 00:32:49,092
[sighs]

421
00:32:51,261 --> 00:32:53,305
You're not referring the case
for prosecution?

422
00:32:53,930 --> 00:32:55,891
The victim won't just sit back
and take it.

423
00:32:57,517 --> 00:33:00,979
In a sexual assault case with no evidence,
what's the first criterion

424
00:33:01,062 --> 00:33:03,440
for determining whether
the victim's statement is credible?

425
00:33:04,566 --> 00:33:06,651
- Consistency.
- Second?

426
00:33:08,278 --> 00:33:10,780
[stammers] I'll go move the car first.

427
00:33:10,864 --> 00:33:12,782
That little… Second?

428
00:33:12,866 --> 00:33:13,867
[groans]

429
00:33:13,950 --> 00:33:15,952
- Second.
- Oh, right.

430
00:33:16,453 --> 00:33:19,456
"Does this make sense logically?"
So, reasonableness.

431
00:33:19,539 --> 00:33:20,832
Third.

432
00:33:20,916 --> 00:33:22,417
[stammers] Third…

433
00:33:23,001 --> 00:33:26,338
We still haven't found any motive
for her to give a false statement.

434
00:33:27,130 --> 00:33:30,258
Let's say her statement,
as the alleged victim, was consistent.

435
00:33:30,342 --> 00:33:32,052
But it isn't reasonable.

436
00:33:32,552 --> 00:33:34,638
- Let's assume she's lying.
- [♪ unsettling music plays]

437
00:33:34,721 --> 00:33:35,972
<i>Then what do you think?</i>

438
00:33:36,056 --> 00:33:39,434
<i>He's a doctor with money</i>
<i>and a good reputation.</i>

439
00:33:39,517 --> 00:33:42,437
- A perfect target for a big settlement.
- What about a polygraph?

440
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,814
So what if we do one?

441
00:33:44,898 --> 00:33:46,524
It's not admissible as evidence.

442
00:33:49,027 --> 00:33:50,195
[footsteps approaching]

443
00:33:57,035 --> 00:33:58,995
[♪ tense music plays]

444
00:33:59,079 --> 00:34:00,455
How can he be found innocent?

445
00:34:00,956 --> 00:34:04,793
Innocence is for the court to decide.
That's not our determination to make.

446
00:34:06,127 --> 00:34:08,755
We're closing the case
without referring it for prosecution.

447
00:34:08,838 --> 00:34:12,300
There's insufficient evidence,
so it's being closed with no charges.

448
00:34:12,384 --> 00:34:14,761
No charges? How does that make any sense?

449
00:34:14,844 --> 00:34:17,639
Min Junho washed the wine glasses.
Why would he have done that?

450
00:34:19,808 --> 00:34:21,142
Why do you think he did it?

451
00:34:21,226 --> 00:34:22,352
To destroy the evidence.

452
00:34:23,144 --> 00:34:26,940
- He must've drugged me. I'm sure of it.
- As you know…

453
00:34:28,650 --> 00:34:30,568
your blood test didn't show anything.

454
00:34:30,652 --> 00:34:32,570
GHB. The date-rape drug!

455
00:34:35,740 --> 00:34:38,994
I'm the victim. How could you let him go
without even saying a word to me?

456
00:34:39,077 --> 00:34:41,997
The police aren't required
to get the victim's consent

457
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:43,665
before making that decision.

458
00:34:44,291 --> 00:34:47,585
If you'd like,
you can file a request for disclosure.

459
00:34:55,468 --> 00:34:56,469
You people…

460
00:34:57,429 --> 00:34:59,556
Would you do this
if it happened to your family?

461
00:35:00,807 --> 00:35:03,643
How can you not be angry
about something like this?

462
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:06,855
I understand how you feel, but…

463
00:35:08,857 --> 00:35:11,860
this is the outcome based on
investigative principles and procedures.

464
00:35:16,323 --> 00:35:18,992
Nothing is ever
completely someone else's problem.

465
00:35:22,537 --> 00:35:24,497
You'll understand once it happens to you.

466
00:35:26,875 --> 00:35:28,376
Please apologize before you leave.

467
00:35:28,460 --> 00:35:30,587
You should apologize to me first!

468
00:35:42,307 --> 00:35:44,392
[door opens, closes]

469
00:35:44,934 --> 00:35:47,228
[team leader] She just threatened
a police officer, right?

470
00:35:55,737 --> 00:35:56,905
[inhales sharply]

471
00:35:56,988 --> 00:35:57,989
[phone buzzing]

472
00:36:03,078 --> 00:36:06,039
INCOMING CALL
JUNGHYEON

473
00:36:12,170 --> 00:36:15,799
[Jisun] Do you know how women can avoid
being sexually assaulted in the summer?

474
00:36:21,262 --> 00:36:23,431
I don't know. Watch what they wear?

475
00:36:25,433 --> 00:36:26,726
There's no way.

476
00:36:30,563 --> 00:36:33,358
Just like it's not a child's fault
when they're sexually abused,

477
00:36:34,818 --> 00:36:37,404
anyone can be sexually assaulted
if they're unlucky enough.

478
00:36:39,739 --> 00:36:41,908
- Well, of course.
- But see?

479
00:36:45,704 --> 00:36:47,163
You just said it was the clothes,

480
00:36:47,247 --> 00:36:49,290
like the victim somehow
brought it themselves.

481
00:36:54,629 --> 00:36:57,215
Don't treat everyone you know
like they're a criminal.

482
00:36:58,216 --> 00:36:59,592
I want to kill that bastard too.

483
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:01,511
[footsteps approaching]

484
00:37:09,310 --> 00:37:11,229
You said you had something to tell me.

485
00:37:12,272 --> 00:37:13,565
It's about Min Junho.

486
00:37:17,527 --> 00:37:18,737
What?

487
00:37:21,823 --> 00:37:24,033
[whispering] Do you know
how that bastard's wife died?

488
00:37:24,117 --> 00:37:26,119
[♪ haunting music plays]

489
00:37:31,499 --> 00:37:33,376
<i>She took her own life, an overdose.</i>

490
00:37:37,088 --> 00:37:38,798
- No way.
- [Junghyeon] Yeah.

491
00:37:40,759 --> 00:37:43,928
Apparently, she had depression.
I mean, he's a doctor.

492
00:37:44,012 --> 00:37:46,222
Unless he let it happen,
or it was intentional…

493
00:37:47,140 --> 00:37:49,642
Drugs to commit a crime
and a wife dead from an overdose.

494
00:37:49,726 --> 00:37:51,519
Isn't that too much of a coincidence?

495
00:37:54,314 --> 00:37:56,524
He's a doctor,
but psychiatry isn't his specialty.

496
00:37:56,608 --> 00:37:58,193
And he'd still need a prescription.

497
00:37:58,276 --> 00:38:01,863
Whenever a medical facility closes,
it's always the drugs that go missing.

498
00:38:02,614 --> 00:38:05,492
If a medical professional is determined,
there's no stopping them.

499
00:38:08,745 --> 00:38:12,415
<i>Who knows what kind of drugs that bastard</i>
<i>might have hidden in his house?</i>

500
00:38:16,461 --> 00:38:19,672
I don't want to drag a dead person
into this just to tie it to my case.

501
00:38:20,673 --> 00:38:22,217
I'll pretend I never heard that.

502
00:38:45,365 --> 00:38:46,366
Here.

503
00:38:49,077 --> 00:38:50,954
Enough with the attitude.

504
00:38:53,915 --> 00:38:54,958
I said, that's enough.

505
00:38:55,041 --> 00:38:56,125
Why were you arrested?

506
00:39:01,381 --> 00:39:04,342
I heard you got arrested at the hospital.
Why did they arrest you?

507
00:39:06,719 --> 00:39:09,305
- Who told you that?
- I'm asking you why they arrested you!

508
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:16,729
Hyunsoo.

509
00:39:18,439 --> 00:39:21,985
"Dad, someone told me
something like that happened."

510
00:39:22,485 --> 00:39:24,988
"Is that true?" That's how you should ask.

511
00:39:27,866 --> 00:39:29,200
Are you a sex offender?

512
00:39:44,632 --> 00:39:48,469
I met this woman.

513
00:39:55,268 --> 00:39:57,270
And I thought she was a good person.

514
00:39:58,688 --> 00:40:00,148
I thought maybe she could even be

515
00:40:01,149 --> 00:40:03,026
a good mom to you.

516
00:40:06,195 --> 00:40:07,739
I don't need a mom.

517
00:40:08,323 --> 00:40:09,324
[smacks lips]

518
00:40:11,701 --> 00:40:14,370
The first time I asked her out on a date,
she turned me down.

519
00:40:15,163 --> 00:40:16,956
The second time, she said yes.

520
00:40:18,750 --> 00:40:21,085
- So we had dinner together…
- [♪ gentle music plays]

521
00:40:21,169 --> 00:40:26,507
…went to her place,
had some wine, and talked…

522
00:40:27,759 --> 00:40:29,844
We had a good time.

523
00:40:32,597 --> 00:40:34,182
She was the first…

524
00:40:37,226 --> 00:40:38,478
since your mom.

525
00:40:45,151 --> 00:40:46,778
Then I came home.

526
00:40:50,949 --> 00:40:52,116
That's it?

527
00:40:54,535 --> 00:40:55,536
[Junho] Yeah.

528
00:40:57,538 --> 00:40:59,499
But the next day,
the police came to see me.

529
00:41:01,626 --> 00:41:03,169
They said I'd done something wrong.

530
00:41:11,928 --> 00:41:13,388
I was questioned by the police,

531
00:41:15,098 --> 00:41:17,225
and they let me go
because they found nothing.

532
00:41:17,809 --> 00:41:19,727
Then why would she do that?

533
00:41:21,646 --> 00:41:22,814
I don't know.

534
00:41:24,357 --> 00:41:25,483
Maybe…

535
00:41:27,026 --> 00:41:29,654
there was something she wanted from me.

536
00:41:31,656 --> 00:41:32,657
Money?

537
00:41:33,324 --> 00:41:34,534
Probably.

538
00:41:36,703 --> 00:41:37,704
[sighs]

539
00:41:38,246 --> 00:41:39,706
She's a bad person.

540
00:41:43,501 --> 00:41:45,878
[Junho] Remember when you went
to the police station

541
00:41:46,921 --> 00:41:51,259
after you got caught trying to
sell those fake sneakers?

542
00:41:54,387 --> 00:41:57,598
I knew you didn't do it.

543
00:42:00,435 --> 00:42:01,769
How did you know?

544
00:42:03,396 --> 00:42:04,522
Because I trust you.

545
00:42:06,858 --> 00:42:08,526
I know my son isn't that kind of kid.

546
00:42:10,778 --> 00:42:13,406
You probably trusted me too.

547
00:42:13,489 --> 00:42:17,035
That's why you felt betrayed
and started acting out like that.

548
00:42:17,869 --> 00:42:18,870
[sighs]

549
00:42:19,412 --> 00:42:20,413
Still,

550
00:42:21,831 --> 00:42:23,708
everyone at school knows.

551
00:42:33,217 --> 00:42:34,218
Min Hyunsoo.

552
00:42:35,261 --> 00:42:36,763
Hold your head high.

553
00:42:38,181 --> 00:42:40,224
I'm a victim, and so are you.

554
00:42:42,518 --> 00:42:46,606
<i>Victims have to hold their heads high</i>
<i>for there to be any justice in this world.</i>

555
00:42:50,068 --> 00:42:52,070
[♪ soft music plays]

556
00:43:13,299 --> 00:43:14,509
Good morning.

557
00:43:36,781 --> 00:43:38,116
[phone buzzes]

558
00:43:47,250 --> 00:43:48,251
[door lock chimes]

559
00:43:54,590 --> 00:43:56,843
Looks like you didn't sleep well.

560
00:43:57,677 --> 00:43:58,719
Why?

561
00:44:00,221 --> 00:44:03,349
You think insomnia might make me
mistake a date for a crime?

562
00:44:08,396 --> 00:44:10,565
I've handled a lot of cases like this.

563
00:44:13,067 --> 00:44:15,820
So I can usually tell right away
if someone is really a victim.

564
00:44:18,531 --> 00:44:20,992
It's a kind of instinct I've developed.

565
00:44:26,455 --> 00:44:28,124
But with this case…

566
00:44:30,543 --> 00:44:32,003
Honestly, it's hard to tell.

567
00:44:35,256 --> 00:44:36,507
[Junho] <i>A toxicology screening?</i>

568
00:44:38,176 --> 00:44:39,177
Did Jisun ask for it?

569
00:44:40,052 --> 00:44:41,053
It's a routine test.

570
00:44:41,137 --> 00:44:45,099
There's nothing routine about
treating your date like a drug offender.

571
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:49,937
You're not asking what the results were.

572
00:44:52,982 --> 00:44:56,861
<i>Mr. Min didn't care about</i>
<i>the test results at all.</i>

573
00:44:59,864 --> 00:45:02,783
One of you is clearly lying.

574
00:45:04,243 --> 00:45:05,870
But it's not just a lie.

575
00:45:07,747 --> 00:45:09,957
It's intricately woven into the truth.

576
00:45:18,716 --> 00:45:20,885
Isn't there any way
to find out who's lying?

577
00:45:27,141 --> 00:45:30,144
Would you be willing to take a polygraph?

578
00:45:30,853 --> 00:45:32,855
[door slides open]

579
00:45:36,776 --> 00:45:38,361
[Jisun] <i>He'll do it too, right?</i>

580
00:45:40,238 --> 00:45:41,280
[Junho] What's going on?

581
00:45:43,032 --> 00:45:44,158
[nurse] Oh.

582
00:45:44,242 --> 00:45:47,245
We were told Dr. An
would be performing the surgery.

583
00:45:51,207 --> 00:45:52,208
[Junho sighs]

584
00:46:12,186 --> 00:46:13,229
Dr. Kang.

585
00:46:18,150 --> 00:46:20,695
- Can you tell your sister--
- Don't talk about my sister.

586
00:46:20,778 --> 00:46:22,405
No, please make sure you tell her this.

587
00:46:24,699 --> 00:46:25,908
[Jieun sighs]

588
00:46:25,992 --> 00:46:27,493
I don't know why she's doing this,

589
00:46:28,452 --> 00:46:29,453
but that night…

590
00:46:31,497 --> 00:46:32,623
I was really happy.

591
00:46:34,917 --> 00:46:37,503
I've probably told more lies
than I can count in my life.

592
00:46:39,255 --> 00:46:40,756
But I meant what I just said.

593
00:46:45,761 --> 00:46:46,887
[Junho exhales deeply]

594
00:46:50,224 --> 00:46:53,060
Don't perform surgery, don't do rounds.

595
00:46:53,144 --> 00:46:55,229
Are you telling me to leave the hospital?

596
00:46:58,065 --> 00:47:01,068
- Director. The investigation is over.
- [door opens]

597
00:47:01,152 --> 00:47:03,487
I was cleared.
There are no charges against me.

598
00:47:05,906 --> 00:47:07,783
I was falsely accused.
I'm the victim here.

599
00:47:07,867 --> 00:47:09,952
How does that damage
the hospital's reputation?

600
00:47:12,371 --> 00:47:13,372
[exhales sharply]

601
00:47:15,750 --> 00:47:16,751
Okay, I understand.

602
00:47:18,461 --> 00:47:19,628
[call ends]

603
00:47:19,712 --> 00:47:22,673
Your Mr. Perfect image
is completely ruined.

604
00:47:23,674 --> 00:47:25,926
Oh, wait. It's not just an image.

605
00:47:26,010 --> 00:47:27,428
You really are Mr. Perfect.

606
00:47:29,180 --> 00:47:31,098
You got played by a gold digger,
didn't you?

607
00:47:32,141 --> 00:47:33,267
That's not what happened.

608
00:47:33,351 --> 00:47:36,562
[scoffs] Don't be so naive.

609
00:47:37,521 --> 00:47:41,108
People like us get respected around here.

610
00:47:41,192 --> 00:47:44,111
But out there, we're just suckers
waiting to be taken advantage of.

611
00:47:46,322 --> 00:47:47,740
I trust people.

612
00:47:48,491 --> 00:47:49,784
And this isn't a big deal.

613
00:47:51,202 --> 00:47:52,203
All right.

614
00:47:52,286 --> 00:47:54,455
That's probably why
you were released so quickly.

615
00:47:54,538 --> 00:47:55,748
Don't worry too much.

616
00:47:55,831 --> 00:47:58,292
The hospital's busy,
and people forget things fast.

617
00:47:58,918 --> 00:48:02,463
But since the director gave the order,
stay out of the OR for a while.

618
00:48:03,297 --> 00:48:05,424
And you might want to look
into other hospitals.

619
00:48:06,008 --> 00:48:07,093
Good luck.

620
00:48:12,306 --> 00:48:13,307
[sighs]

621
00:48:14,767 --> 00:48:16,519
[phone buzzing]

622
00:48:23,234 --> 00:48:24,235
Hello?

623
00:48:27,696 --> 00:48:30,574
Is there anything left for us to discuss?

624
00:48:33,119 --> 00:48:36,455
Why did you wash the wine glasses?

625
00:48:37,123 --> 00:48:38,124
[scoffs]

626
00:48:39,333 --> 00:48:42,586
Why leave out the fact
that I washed the cheese plate too?

627
00:48:47,007 --> 00:48:49,969
As you know,
I take care of my own household.

628
00:48:50,719 --> 00:48:54,306
So I'm in the habit of washing dishes
as soon as I see them.

629
00:48:55,766 --> 00:48:57,518
The next day was a weekday,

630
00:48:57,601 --> 00:49:01,397
and I thought Ms. Kang might be busy
in the morning, so I washed them.

631
00:49:02,356 --> 00:49:03,732
What, is that illegal too?

632
00:49:06,110 --> 00:49:07,111
No.

633
00:49:13,325 --> 00:49:17,872
Medical care is built on trust
between a doctor and a patient.

634
00:49:18,497 --> 00:49:21,709
But now my whole life is falling apart.

635
00:49:22,376 --> 00:49:25,754
How far is this going to go?
How long is this going to keep happening?

636
00:49:28,007 --> 00:49:32,386
I'm asking for your understanding until
the investigation is officially closed.

637
00:49:35,097 --> 00:49:36,098
[sighs]

638
00:49:39,226 --> 00:49:41,437
You could file
a false accusation complaint

639
00:49:41,520 --> 00:49:45,024
and prove your innocence.

640
00:49:45,107 --> 00:49:46,942
She's my son's teacher.

641
00:49:48,360 --> 00:49:49,653
For his sake,

642
00:49:50,905 --> 00:49:53,240
I don't want to make this
any bigger than it already is.

643
00:49:55,701 --> 00:49:58,746
Ms. Kang doesn't seem
to feel the same way.

644
00:50:02,500 --> 00:50:04,877
- <i>She's agreed to take a polygraph.</i>
- [♪ soft, tense music plays]

645
00:50:05,544 --> 00:50:09,381
<i>Your statements conflict,</i>
<i>so if the results support her account,</i>

646
00:50:09,965 --> 00:50:12,343
we'll probably reopen
the investigation based on that.

647
00:50:13,427 --> 00:50:17,306
Polygraph results aren't even admissible
as evidence in court.

648
00:50:17,806 --> 00:50:21,852
They can be used as indirect evidence
depending on the circumstances.

649
00:50:23,604 --> 00:50:28,984
The truth should be judged by
a person's conscience, not by a machine.

650
00:50:30,486 --> 00:50:32,655
I don't believe we should hand over

651
00:50:33,155 --> 00:50:35,366
even the last shred of human dignity
to a machine.

652
00:50:35,449 --> 00:50:38,202
It's more science than machine.

653
00:50:38,285 --> 00:50:39,578
And it's fairly accurate.

654
00:50:42,498 --> 00:50:43,791
[Junho] I'm a doctor.

655
00:50:43,874 --> 00:50:47,586
When someone lies,
a certain psychological change occurs,

656
00:50:48,087 --> 00:50:52,049
and that change has to produce
a corresponding physiological response.

657
00:50:53,300 --> 00:50:56,887
But those changes and responses
can never be consistent.

658
00:50:59,056 --> 00:51:00,641
In the end, it's just statistics.

659
00:51:03,644 --> 00:51:05,229
Statistics is science too.

660
00:51:07,189 --> 00:51:10,359
If you have nothing to hide,
why not take the test?

661
00:51:11,277 --> 00:51:12,736
If you haven't lied,

662
00:51:12,820 --> 00:51:15,155
it could help show
that you didn't commit any crimes.

663
00:51:15,864 --> 00:51:17,408
I haven't lied about anything.

664
00:51:18,284 --> 00:51:19,326
Exactly.

665
00:51:22,871 --> 00:51:26,292
- [button clicks]
- [examiner] Is your name Kang Jisun?

666
00:51:27,418 --> 00:51:28,752
[button clicks]

667
00:51:28,836 --> 00:51:29,837
Yes.

668
00:51:33,340 --> 00:51:35,718
[examiner]
Are you a contract teacher-librarian?

669
00:51:37,136 --> 00:51:38,137
Yes.

670
00:51:38,762 --> 00:51:40,889
[examiner] Have you ever been married?

671
00:51:42,558 --> 00:51:43,684
No.

672
00:51:46,061 --> 00:51:47,062
[mic feedback]

673
00:51:48,522 --> 00:51:51,442
[examiner]
Were you attracted to Mr. Min Junho?

674
00:51:53,110 --> 00:51:54,862
[♪ tense music plays]

675
00:51:54,945 --> 00:51:59,575
WERE YOU ATTRACTED
TO MR. MIN JUNHO?

676
00:52:04,204 --> 00:52:05,456
[polygraph beeping]

677
00:52:13,297 --> 00:52:14,590
Yes, at first.

678
00:52:17,635 --> 00:52:18,636
[Junho] <i>But…</i>

679
00:52:19,553 --> 00:52:20,554
<i>I am curious.</i>

680
00:52:25,392 --> 00:52:27,144
People don't believe me.

681
00:52:27,936 --> 00:52:29,480
But I wonder if a machine will.

682
00:52:31,065 --> 00:52:32,816
- Then…
- Let's do it.

683
00:52:33,817 --> 00:52:35,152
The polygraph.

684
00:52:40,824 --> 00:52:43,494
[examiner] Is your name Min Junho?

685
00:52:43,577 --> 00:52:44,578
[button clicks]

686
00:52:45,329 --> 00:52:46,330
Yes.

687
00:52:48,165 --> 00:52:50,501
- [button clicks]
- [examiner] Are you a doctor?

688
00:52:53,671 --> 00:52:55,339
Yes, I'm a cardiovascular surgeon.

689
00:52:58,801 --> 00:53:00,594
Are you homosexual?

690
00:53:03,013 --> 00:53:04,056
No.

691
00:53:05,974 --> 00:53:09,395
[examiner] Do you have any memories
of being sexually harassed as a child?

692
00:53:11,730 --> 00:53:13,023
Yes. In middle school.

693
00:53:14,983 --> 00:53:16,193
[examiner] Was that the first time?

694
00:53:22,074 --> 00:53:23,075
Yes.

695
00:53:25,327 --> 00:53:29,790
My sister was away on a school trip,
so I went home alone that day.

696
00:53:35,963 --> 00:53:38,340
[examiner] <i>Did you know any of them?</i>

697
00:53:40,384 --> 00:53:42,845
[Jisun]
<i>I don't know. It was a long time ago.</i>

698
00:53:44,513 --> 00:53:45,973
<i>They were from the neighborhood,</i>

699
00:53:46,056 --> 00:53:47,641
so I probably saw them around.

700
00:53:53,856 --> 00:53:58,444
[examiner] Do you want revenge on the boys
who sexually harassed you back then?

701
00:54:00,654 --> 00:54:01,780
Revenge?

702
00:54:08,036 --> 00:54:10,122
[examiner]
Do you want them to be punished?

703
00:54:14,501 --> 00:54:17,546
I want them to know exactly what they did.

704
00:54:21,717 --> 00:54:23,802
[examiner] Are you angry at Mr. Min Junho?

705
00:54:23,886 --> 00:54:26,388
ARE YOU ANGRY AT MR. MIN JUNHO
AT THE MOMENT?

706
00:54:31,059 --> 00:54:32,060
Yes.

707
00:54:36,315 --> 00:54:39,026
Do you want to kill Min Junho?

708
00:54:40,277 --> 00:54:41,278
[polygraph beeping]

709
00:54:56,168 --> 00:54:58,170
IS THERE ANY EVENT
FROM YOUR CHILDHOOD

710
00:54:58,253 --> 00:55:00,214
THAT STANDS OUT IN YOUR MEMORY?

711
00:55:00,297 --> 00:55:01,715
When I was nine.

712
00:55:03,342 --> 00:55:08,972
A kitten was sitting by the window,
looking at me.

713
00:55:13,560 --> 00:55:15,103
[examiner] <i>What did you do?</i>

714
00:55:17,356 --> 00:55:19,358
I opened the window for it.

715
00:55:22,611 --> 00:55:24,530
[examiner] Did the kitten ever come back?

716
00:55:27,032 --> 00:55:28,033
No.

717
00:55:31,828 --> 00:55:37,876
The kitten ate the chocolate
I gave it that day and died.

718
00:55:49,346 --> 00:55:51,223
[polygraph beeping]

719
00:56:18,709 --> 00:56:20,043
[sniffles]

720
00:56:20,127 --> 00:56:23,714
[examiner] Did you feel sexual urges
toward Ms. Kang Jisun?

721
00:56:28,552 --> 00:56:29,553
Yes.

722
00:56:30,929 --> 00:56:35,225
[examiner] Do you remember seeing the
kitten dead after eating the chocolate?

723
00:56:41,690 --> 00:56:42,691
Yes.

724
00:56:50,115 --> 00:56:53,910
Did you sexually assault her that night?

725
00:57:09,551 --> 00:57:11,678
[detective retching]

726
00:57:14,890 --> 00:57:16,391
- [sighs]
- [toilet flushes]

727
00:57:18,477 --> 00:57:19,478
[sighs]

728
00:57:28,570 --> 00:57:31,740
After breakfast, puke. After lunch, puke.

729
00:57:31,823 --> 00:57:35,160
[spouse] <i>I need to have a word</i>
<i>with Chubchubs. Let me see.</i>

730
00:57:38,205 --> 00:57:40,540
<i>Chubchubs, Daddy's coming home real soon.</i>

731
00:57:40,624 --> 00:57:43,543
<i>Until then,</i>
<i>don't give my woman a hard time.</i>

732
00:57:43,627 --> 00:57:45,754
How about you? How's the food?

733
00:57:45,837 --> 00:57:48,131
<i>I'm always eating well.</i>

734
00:57:48,215 --> 00:57:49,508
<i>The Navy food's pretty good.</i>

735
00:57:50,342 --> 00:57:54,096
<i>But anyway, what if my Hwayoung gets weak</i>
<i>from not being able to eat?</i>

736
00:57:54,179 --> 00:57:56,890
Well, I blend up anything
that's supposed to be good for me

737
00:57:56,973 --> 00:57:59,726
and drink it as juice,
so I should be getting enough nutrition.

738
00:57:59,810 --> 00:58:02,688
NEW EMAIL

739
00:58:02,771 --> 00:58:03,772
[spouse] <i>What is it?</i>

740
00:58:05,315 --> 00:58:07,484
I got an important email
about an investigation.

741
00:58:07,984 --> 00:58:12,989
POLYGRAPH TEST RESULTS

742
00:58:14,741 --> 00:58:15,742
[clicks mouse]

743
00:58:19,663 --> 00:58:20,664
[sighs]

744
00:58:26,878 --> 00:58:28,130
[Hwayoung exhales deeply]

745
00:58:30,257 --> 00:58:31,550
Where have you been?

746
00:58:31,633 --> 00:58:32,926
I was feeling a bit sick.

747
00:58:35,011 --> 00:58:36,221
[whispering] Can you tell?

748
00:58:36,304 --> 00:58:37,472
Pretty obvious.

749
00:58:39,933 --> 00:58:42,269
Secrets don't stay secret
for long around here.

750
00:58:43,562 --> 00:58:45,480
If I get caught, I'll have to spill.

751
00:58:45,564 --> 00:58:48,984
[sighs] I don't know
if this will make you feel any better.

752
00:58:49,067 --> 00:58:52,070
But my wife was sick for all nine months
when she was pregnant.

753
00:58:52,154 --> 00:58:53,405
[Hwayoung chuckles]

754
00:58:53,488 --> 00:58:55,490
That's a really cruel way
to comfort someone.

755
00:58:55,991 --> 00:58:57,284
You know me. I don't lie.

756
00:58:57,951 --> 00:59:01,413
Oh, right. Did you tell them
about the polygraph results?

757
00:59:04,833 --> 00:59:06,376
Geez.

758
00:59:06,460 --> 00:59:09,087
You can never really know
what someone is thinking.

759
00:59:13,675 --> 00:59:17,095
I barely eat at home.
Why did he make so many side dishes?

760
00:59:17,179 --> 00:59:18,555
You know he always goes overboard.

761
00:59:20,015 --> 00:59:21,850
Tell Hyeongsu I said thanks.

762
00:59:21,933 --> 00:59:23,185
How are you sleeping?

763
00:59:23,852 --> 00:59:25,187
Are you getting any sleep?

764
00:59:27,147 --> 00:59:28,190
Well, you know…

765
00:59:30,525 --> 00:59:33,737
If you don't want to be alone,
come stay with us anytime.

766
00:59:33,820 --> 00:59:35,197
Hyeongsu said the same.

767
00:59:36,782 --> 00:59:39,367
You'll marry Hyeongsu again
in your next life, right?

768
00:59:43,121 --> 00:59:45,499
[doorbell rings]

769
00:59:50,462 --> 00:59:52,380
Looks like
you're going to have to hire me.

770
00:59:59,971 --> 01:00:00,972
[door closes]

771
01:00:11,024 --> 01:00:14,194
The polygraph results are in.

772
01:00:17,989 --> 01:00:19,908
[attorney]
<i>Something similar happened at the school</i>

773
01:00:19,991 --> 01:00:21,368
<i>where she worked before moving here.</i>

774
01:00:21,868 --> 01:00:25,330
She accused some guy of sexual harassment
and completely ruined his life.

775
01:00:25,413 --> 01:00:29,000
PURPOSE OF COMPLAINT
THE COMPLAINANT HEREBY FILES…

776
01:00:29,084 --> 01:00:31,086
- [♪ tense music plays]
- [objects clattering]

777
01:00:34,005 --> 01:00:36,174
Hey, do you only have rabbit food
in your fridge?

778
01:00:41,638 --> 01:00:45,267
[Hwayoung] <i>The analysis found</i>
<i>that all of Mr. Min Junho's statements</i>

779
01:00:46,059 --> 01:00:48,436
were truthful.

780
01:00:51,022 --> 01:00:53,859
- [♪ unsettling music plays]
- [attorney] <i>She's relentless.</i>

781
01:00:53,942 --> 01:00:56,653
She kept at it until the bitter end
and eventually walked away

782
01:00:56,736 --> 01:00:58,196
with a settlement.

783
01:00:59,948 --> 01:01:01,408
You got played by that woman.

784
01:01:07,998 --> 01:01:10,542
You need to fight back
and not drag your feet.

785
01:01:10,625 --> 01:01:12,252
Or she'll ruin your life too.

786
01:01:15,130 --> 01:01:17,716
- That can't be true.
- You think the truth matters?

787
01:01:17,799 --> 01:01:19,009
What matters is the rumor.

788
01:01:20,051 --> 01:01:21,219
Look around you.

789
01:01:21,303 --> 01:01:23,722
No one cares about the truth.
Reputation comes first.

790
01:01:24,806 --> 01:01:26,850
- She's not that kind of woman.
- Yes, she is.

791
01:01:27,893 --> 01:01:30,729
She's a repeat offender
who plays the victim for money.

792
01:01:34,274 --> 01:01:35,567
What does that mean?

793
01:01:35,650 --> 01:01:37,152
Exactly what I said.

794
01:01:38,737 --> 01:01:40,906
Mr. Min Junho wasn't lying.

795
01:01:44,659 --> 01:01:45,702
How is that possible?

796
01:01:45,785 --> 01:01:48,413
People can remember and interpret
the same event differently

797
01:01:48,914 --> 01:01:51,249
depending on their perspective.

798
01:01:56,796 --> 01:01:58,840
I'll tell you your results too.

799
01:01:58,924 --> 01:02:01,593
- Well, of course--
- [Hwayoung] Ms. Kang, your statements…

800
01:02:03,762 --> 01:02:06,056
showed signs of deception.

801
01:02:06,806 --> 01:02:07,807
[♪ music stops]

802
01:02:13,104 --> 01:02:14,356
[♪ dramatic music plays]

803
01:02:14,439 --> 01:02:15,649
That's impossible.

804
01:02:17,525 --> 01:02:20,487
How could the results be
so completely wrong?

805
01:02:22,864 --> 01:02:25,200
Something's obviously wrong.
It's the exact opposite!

806
01:02:25,283 --> 01:02:28,787
Of the two of you, the one who lied…

807
01:02:33,541 --> 01:02:34,626
is you.

808
01:02:44,594 --> 01:02:48,515
THE PERFECT LIE

809
01:03:12,622 --> 01:03:14,416
[Junho] <i>There must've been a reason.</i>

810
01:03:15,667 --> 01:03:17,627
[Jisun] You want me to admit I lied? Now?

811
01:03:18,503 --> 01:03:20,797
[Junho] <i>Maybe there's something</i>
<i>wrong with her psychologically.</i>

812
01:03:20,880 --> 01:03:23,008
- [Hyunsoo] <i>That woman was you?</i>
- [doorbell rings]

813
01:03:24,259 --> 01:03:25,885
[attorney]
<i>She isn't going to let this go easily.</i>

814
01:03:25,969 --> 01:03:29,055
[Jisun] How am I supposed to have a life
after he ruined me like this?

815
01:03:29,139 --> 01:03:32,434
[Junho] <i>What you did impulsively…</i>
<i>You're trying to dump all the blame on me.</i>

816
01:03:32,517 --> 01:03:35,061
[Jisun] <i>I'm going to ask them</i>
<i>to reinvestigate everything.</i>

817
01:03:35,145 --> 01:03:38,314
[attorney] <i>They say an anonymous woman</i>
<i>tipped them off. It's obvious who it was.</i>

818
01:03:38,398 --> 01:03:40,275
[Junho] <i>You got caught lying to me.</i>

819
01:03:41,151 --> 01:03:42,902
And now you're asking me to lie too?

820
01:03:48,825 --> 01:03:50,326
[♪ unsettling music plays]

821
01:03:59,044 --> 01:04:00,670
THE PERFECT LIE

822
01:04:00,754 --> 01:04:02,756
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi3
